{# Guidance Layer #}
Review two alternative future plans. The original is a valid choice; keep it unless the candidate offers clear benefit. Choose one, never merge both.
Check motivation, causality, unresolved promises, explicit user requirements and accepted facts. Future events may change; established events, knowledge and resources may not.
Every passed check needs specific input evidence. Insufficient information fails the check. Synchronized contracts must cover changes without silently abandoning promises or locked points. Explain creative_gain through novelty and naturalness, not imagery or number frequency.
